A||||30||FieroRyan||Mr. Mikes Leather Seats||||1||
Z||000000||FieroRyan||09-07-2001||04:41 AM||||I ordered mine a few days ago, and I was just wondering how easy the install is, and what all is involved...  anyone else here get them?  Are they great?  <P><BR>Thanks!<BR>Ryan<P>------------------<BR>I love my Fiero :D||||reg||1
Z||000001||Denny||09-07-2001||05:38 AM||||Love mine!  And they're a big hit wherever I go. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I did mine in one evening, in my livivng room.<P>Took about 4 hours total, including removing the seats from the car and re-installing.<P>You'll love them, too!||||reg||10
Z||000002||Oreif||09-07-2001||08:21 AM||||I have had mine for 2 years. They are great. As for installing them, It's about 1.5 to 2 hours per seat. Just follow the instruction video. It is easy to follow and do.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-07-2001||10:27 AM||||Same here. 1st seat took me 2 hrs. Second 30 minutes (learning curve).||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||09-07-2001||10:58 AM||||They're impossible to install. In fact, to save you further pain and embarassment, you should just mail them to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>I'll be finding out first-hand in a week or so - getting ready to order a set for the car Dad and I share. Every time I've heard comments about Mr. Mike and/or his stuff, it's been absoluitely nothing but 100% praise, so I'm looking forward to supporting his craft.<P>I may end up getting some for the Formula a year or so down the road so I can save my near-perfect stock seats for car shows... <P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||09-07-2001||04:13 PM||||Interesting you should post this question, because I was just last night considering this very subject.  The prices I saw on Mr. Mike's website <B>did</B> seem like a lot of to shell out on one just item for my car.<P>But then, I called a reputable upholsterer here in town the other day, and they estimated $225 to reupholster, <B>per</B> seat!  That's not leather, either.<P>Suddenly, I'm thinking, $200 per seat for Mr. Mikes two-tones gets me leather seats, plus the experience of doing it myself, sounds like a good deal after all.  And, like the others have posted, I don't think I have <B>ever</B> heard (or, read) a discouraging word regarding Mr. Mike's.  Everyone here that has tried it, seems to be very pleased with the results.  Now, for me, it's not a question of "if", but "when."  And of course the tougher questions - color, style, etc.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>        ||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnF||09-07-2001||06:18 PM||||FYI - your "reputable upholsterer" is holding you up!  About 6 months ago, I got tired of sitting on duct tape and decided to get the driver's set redone to factory specs.  OEM cloth/vinyl (med. gray) complete replacement (including seat removal/replacement, padding and all labor) drive-out price $125.00.  Looks and feels like the passenger (cup holder's side) - like new!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-07-2001||06:53 PM||||JohnF--You should consider yourself lucky.  My local upholsterer quoted me over $600 for the pair of seats.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
