Z||000014||Ed||09-08-2001||12:15 AM||||Another satisfied customer.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Boomtastic||09-08-2001||05:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroRyan:<BR><B>I ordered mine a few days ago, and I was just wondering how easy the install is, and what all is involved...  anyone else here get them?  Are they great?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mike's video will make you think that you can do the seats in 20 minutes - NOT! It took a few hours, mainly because the rods that hold the seat fabric and/or leather come out easier than they go back in. Prepare to sweat and curse a lot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> BUT, when they are all in and back in the Fiero, you will not believe how great they are! Your bum will thank you for it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Denny||09-08-2001||05:29 AM||||Here's a shot of my Mr. Mike's seats:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCL86se_2.jpg">  <P>And the steering wheel:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_wheel_1.jpg">  <P>I chose light grey/navy for the wheel to match some current components and future mods.<P>And Eric's right about your butt appreciating it!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000017||T-top Fiero||09-08-2001||11:06 AM||||Sloth, Mr. Mikes doesn't advertise the steering wheel recovering. He only recovers the GT 3 spoke steering wheels. They can be recovered in any color of leather he uses for his seats. They can be all one color or the top one color and the bottom another.<BR>He charges around $200 for them.<BR>Here is a picture showing mine.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driversint_1.jpg"> <P>Pat<p>[This message has been edited by T-top Fiero (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
